{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And a king arose.</b> One may say: from the fact that it does not write 'the king died,' this teaches that it was the same king himself, who was already there, except that his decrees were renewed. And what does 'arose' mean? That he rose against Israel as an enemy, as it is said, 'לאור יקום רוצח' (at light the murderer arises), 'כי קמו בי עדי שקר' (for witnesses of falsehood have risen against me)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "י״‎מ resolved as 'one may say' (יש לומר); ש״‎מ resolved as 'this teaches' (ש\"מ = ש\"ל משמע)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:40.658277159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}